    doc = "Firefly Aerospace Blue Ghost Mission 1 lunar lander (landed in Mare Crisium, March 2025): a 2 m tall chamfered-square body in copper MLI with two body-mounted solar panels, four carbon legs with crush-core strokes and saucer footpads, a fixed Nammo LEROS 4-ET main engine, eight Spectre RCS thrusters, twelve cold-gas ACS thrusters and a gimballed X-band panel antenna."
